# 1. PROJECT IDENTITY

**Project name:** SaferShift

**Full title:** Personalized, Privacy-Preserving Driver Safety Intelligence

**Selected problem statement:** Edge-Optimized Driver Fatigue & Distraction Monitor.

**Category:** Computer vision, edge AI, real-time monitoring, personalization, and road safety.

### Project mission

Build an offline driver-monitoring prototype that analyzes facial landmarks over time, calibrates relevant measurements to individual drivers, detects sustained visual indicators of possible fatigue or distraction, explains its warnings, and evaluates whether personalization reduces false alarms.

### The core innovation

Most basic prototypes rely on universal thresholds or classify each frame independently.

SaferShift will implement two comparable detection modes:

1. **Standard mode:** Uses shared, configurable baseline thresholds.
2. **Personalized mode:** Adapts selected thresholds using the driver's own calibration measurements.

Both modes will use the same underlying landmark model and comparable temporal detection logic.

The project's main research question is:

**Can personalized calibration reduce false alarms while preserving the detection of genuine fatigue indicators?**

Treat this as a hypothesis to test. Never assume that personalization improves accuracy before collecting evidence.

